    {
      "label": "Northern Ireland Assembly Elections Order 1982 (S.I. 1982 No. 1135)",
      "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/1982/1135",
      "note": "Made 5 Aug 1982, in operation 6 Sep 1982, under sections 2(5) and 3(3) of the Northern Ireland Assembly Act 1973. Article 2 defines an Assembly constituency, at a general election, as the area that would return a member to the House of Commons if a general election were held that day: on 20 Oct 1982 the constituencies of the Parliamentary Constituencies (Northern Ireland) Order 1970."
    }
